WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.235 --> 00:00:03.235
(upbeat sync music)

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.940
- [Narrator] This, my
friends, is the story

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.500
of the real New Yorker's sandwich

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.350
and the people who keep the legacy alive.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.640
- I've been eating here for 20 years.

00:00:30.793 --> 00:00:32.439
(upbeat jazz music)

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:34.010
- [Narrator] On 110th and 1st Avenue,

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.990
inside the bodega best known
as Hajji's, we meet Salah.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.110
- Yo, boss, let me get two chopped cheese

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.060
with everything on it.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.720
- Lettuce, tomato, pickle, ketchup.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.860
- Put bacon on it, too,
salt, pepper, and vinegar.

00:00:56.769 --> 00:00:59.769
(upbeat jazz music)

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:26.750
- [Narrator] Hajji's is
located in a part of New York

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.020
that's made up of various kinds

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.700
of people with a variety of incomes,

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.410
so keeping chopped cheese at a price point

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.760
everyone can afford has
been a top priority.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.560
In fact, the chopped cheese has only

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.410
gone up a dollar in the last decade.

00:01:51.047 --> 00:01:52.040
- [Narrator] That's why the chopped cheese

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.960
has spread beyond Harlem and
into bodegas far and wide,

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.670
attracting loyal New Yorkers
everywhere it appears.

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:00.780
But in the end, it all comes
back to Hajji's and Salah.

00:02:13.111 --> 00:02:16.111
(mellow rock music)

00:02:21.572 --> 00:02:25.239
(contemplative synth music)

